# Custom modules

Live-server QoL belongs in `modules/custom/`. Enable each file in `modules/init.txt` (`custom/lua/foo.lua`). OK to commit `init.txt` on **`LIVE`** for deploy; never include `init.txt` in LandSandBoat upstream PRs.

## Do

- One concern per feature; artifacts may be `lua/`, `sql/`, `commands/`, and/or `cpp/` with the **same basename** when Lua lacks a core binding (reference: `tutorial_npc_namevis.lua` + `.cpp` + `.sql`).
- Prefer extending an existing related `modules/custom` module over a parallel file for the same concern (e.g. HNM/NM timers → `land_kings.lua`).
- Name `Module:new(...)` to match the filename (snake_case). Prefix `custom_` only if the name could collide with core/era.
- Override the LSB path with `addOverride`. Call `super()` when wrapping. Do not copy whole scripts.
- Label the file as non-retail QoL at the top.
- Module-only settings in `settings/map.lua` or `settings/main.lua` must note the required `init.txt` entry in a comment.
- NM/HNM spawn QoL (windows, ToD persist, no idle/unclaimed despawn) belongs in custom Lua overrides; reference `land_kings.lua`.
- Trash/EXP fast repops (`mob_groups.respawntime`) belong in `modules/custom/sql/faster_repop_times.sql` / `starter_zone_fast_repops.sql` + `init.txt` — not in HNM Lua.
- City rest / town sprint speed QoL belongs in custom Lua overrides; reference `city_rest_quickening.lua`.
- Live-relevant city NPCs hidden by `content_tag = 'SOA'` (Home Points, Artisan/Ephemeral Moogles): clear the tag in `modules/custom/sql/homepoints_live.sql`, not by enabling SoA.
- Live-useful synth gated by `synth_recipes.content_tag` (e.g. guild craft kits buyable but CancelBadRecipe): clear tags in `modules/custom/sql/` (see `guild_craft_kits_live.sql`), not by enabling SoA or removing shop stock.
- RoV-gated trust QoL (Rhapsody slots, Cipher Moogle, alliance trusts): extend `modules/custom/lua/rov_trust_live.lua` — do not flip `ENABLE_ROV` (`custom-module` skill).

## Do not

- Edit `scripts/`, `src/`, repo-root `sql/`, or `modules/era/` for server flavor. Custom SQL belongs in `modules/custom/sql/`.
- Put QoL in `modules/era/` (era is retail reverts only, with content tags).
- Put missing retail features here; those go in core `scripts/` (upstream PR).
- Leave HELM yield multipliers, city rest sprint, land-king QoL, and similar live flavor in core after a cleanup pass — move them here instead.
- Put shortened HNM/NM respawn windows into core `scripts/zones/**/mobs` (e.g. Simurgh/Roc 1–2h in core); use the custom module instead.
- Stack `land_kings` with `custom_HNM_system` / `era_HNM_system`, or put HNM timers into trash-repop SQL.
- Flip `ENABLE_SOA` / loosen `RESTRICT_CONTENT` to restore city QoL NPCs or craft-kit / similar Live QoL — that unlocks Adoulin content Live excludes.

```lua
-----------------------------------
-- Non-retail QoL: Home Points restore HP/MP (single-player style).
-----------------------------------
require('modules/module_utils')
local m = Module:new('homepoint_heal')

m:addOverride('xi.homepoint.onTrigger', function(player, csid, index)
    super(player, csid, index)
end)

return m
```
